# Lane <lane name> — <the one thing this lane is for>

Worker session in its own copy of <repository>, on branch `lane/<item id>`.
Read first: <the two or three files this lane cannot work without>.

**Work item:** `<item id>` — read it, claim it, and at the end resolve it, then
**read it back** with the queue's read command (`work_list`, given the item's
id) and print the stored reason. That printed read-back is the evidence; the
resolve call is not.

**File ownership — edit ONLY:** `<path>/**` and `<path>/**`. Everything else is
off-limits. Never merge to the integration branch. Commit to your branch.

## Outcome

<Two or three sentences describing the state of the world when this lane is
right. Present tense. No steps.>

## Done means exactly ONE of

- **A) SUCCESS** — every acceptance item met, with its evidence visible in a
  committed file or in printed output; the work committed; the item resolved,
  read back, and the stored reason printed. Write
  `<absolute path outside the repository>/DONE.json`:
  `{"status":"success","summary":"…","commits":<n>,"residuals":[…]}`.
- **B) BLOCKED** — a blocker this lane cannot clear. Write
  `<absolute path outside the repository>/BLOCKED.md` naming the cause; commit
  whatever is sound; stop.

No third outcome. If every deliverable is committed and its evidence is on disk
or in printed output, the outcome is A.

